Package: bpfc
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: passwd,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Suggests: bpfc-programs,
Description: eBPF compiler for TC and XDP packet programs, with a daemon
 bpfc compiles a small packet matching and rewriting language straight to
 eBPF bytecode (no LLVM/Clang or libbpf), has the kernel verify it, and
 attaches it to a network interface's TC ingress or egress hook or as its
 XDP program.
 .
 bpfcd keeps the programs in /etc/bpfc/interfaces.d attached: it installs
 them at boot and when interfaces appear, applies changes on reload with an
 atomic replace, and reinstalls or reports programs removed by other tools.
 bpfcctl shows what is installed and from which file. Program files can
 also be Cisco IOS-style access lists (10.acl), translated by a frontend.

Package: bpfc-container
Architecture: all
Depends: bpfc (>= ${source:Version}),
         bpfc (<< ${source:Version}.1~),
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: entrypoint for running bpfcd in a container without systemd
 bpfcd-entrypoint starts bpfcd as a container's main process (PID 1), with
 no systemd. It checks the container's capabilities, prepares bpffs for
 pinned maps and execs bpfcd in the foreground. Includes an example
 Containerfile and run instructions.

Package: bpfc-programs
Architecture: all
Depends: bpfc (>= ${source:Version}),
         bpfc (<< ${source:Version}.1~),
         gawk,
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: programs built on bpfc: dataplane, ECMP, flow and link monitoring
 Everything in the bpfc source tree's programs/ folder: generators and
 status tools that build on bpfc, with their profiles, include files,
 design notes and example programs.
 .
  * dataplane: FEC, ARQ, in-band telemetry and capacity probing for
    point-to-point links, over Layer 2 or UDP (bpfc-dataplane-gen,
    bpfc-dataplane-status)
  * ecmp: bandwidth-aware, policy-based ECMP over the kernel's multipath
    routes (bpfc-ecmp-gen, bpfc-ecmp-status)
  * linkcap: per-neighbor loss, delay and capacity from packet accounting
    (bpfc-linkcap-gen, bpfc-linkcap-status)
  * flowmon: per-flow traffic and TCP retransmission and loss (bpfc-flows)
  * dedup: IPv4 duplicate-packet removal (bpfc-dedup)
  * portscan-guard: port-scan detection and blocking (bpfc-portscanctl)
